# Project-local environment for mastercard-ai-defense-lab.
# Copy this file to .env and fill in real values there. .env is
# gitignored (see .gitignore) -- never commit real secrets.
#
# Used by mandate-demo/'s live agent (mandate_demo/agent.py) and
# web-prototype/'s live-run trigger (web_prototype/live_agent.py) --
# both read OPENAI_API_KEY via the OpenAI SDK's own default (bare
# OpenAI() constructor), which just reads whatever the process
# environment has -- it does not distinguish or prefer a project-local
# value over a machine-wide one. Scoping this key to this project only
# is therefore an operational discipline, not something enforced by the
# code: don't set OPENAI_API_KEY as a Windows user/machine environment
# variable: export this file's contents into your shell instead (or use
# a tool like `direnv` / python-dotenv) each time before running either
# project, so no OpenAI-key state persists outside this shell session.

OPENAI_API_KEY=
